# flyDiy: regenerable model-import intermediates.
# assets/c172/ is produced from assetsSketchfab/free_cessna_172sp.glb (which IS
# committed) by `python tools/glb_extract.py c172`; the baked payload
# src/models/c172_model.js is committed. Contact sheets are scratch.
flyDiy/assets/c172/
flyDiy/tools/_glbview/
# flyDiy renderer probe pages + the previous-commit viewer sources they measure
# against: all written by `node tools/make_probe.js --base`.
flyDiy/tools/_probe.html
flyDiy/tools/_probe_base.html
flyDiy/tools/_base_*.js
# body loft prototypes: judge the fuselage topology before src/core is
# rewritten around them. The CAGE family (tools/_cage_gen.js, _cage_ui.js,
# _cage_fit.js, _cage2/_cage3.html, _cage_ref_*.obj) is TRACKED — it is the
# fuselage rework's foundation (HANDOVER G12). Only the superseded first
# demonstrator stays ignored.
flyDiy/tools/_loft*.html
flyDiy/tools/_wins*.html
flyDiy/tools/_cage.html

# flyDiy: the four REFERENCE aeroplanes whose Sketchfab listing says
# "SKETCHFAB Standard" rather than CC-BY-4.0 (see flyDiy/CREDITS.md). That
# licence does not permit redistribution, and committing either the delivered
# GLB or the baked payload to this public repo IS redistribution. They stay
# local: `python flyDiy/tools/ref_prep.py a22 p68 rv8 sr22` remakes the
# payloads from the GLBs on any machine that has them.
flyDiy/assetsSketchfab/aeroprakt_a22_foxbat.glb
flyDiy/assetsSketchfab/partenavia_p_68.glb
flyDiy/assetsSketchfab/vans_aircraft_rv-8_tail_gear.glb
flyDiy/assetsSketchfab/cirrus_sr_22.glb
flyDiy/src/models/a22_model.js
flyDiy/src/models/p68_model.js
flyDiy/src/models/rv8_model.js
flyDiy/src/models/sr22_model.js
